Actually, since the law of large numbers works against as well as for
you, you'll need to search a lot longer than that to be reasonably sure
that it's a bug. The chance of not finding anything on a single search
when the odds are 1 on 375 is, obviously, 374/375, is about 99.73%. The
chance of not finding anything on N searches with those odds is
(374/375) ^ N. For N=400, that is still more than a third; 34.37%, in
fact. For N=1000, it's just under 7%. To get it down to a statistically
acceptable 5% chance, you need to search 1122 times; to get it to 1%
chance, and therefore 99% certainty that it's a bug, 1725 searches are
needed.

